            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "2. You can play your teams for up to 10 consecutive drawings. Mark the number of \tdraws you want to play in the \u201cDRAWS\u201d section at the bottom of the play slip. Each draw is $5. Your ticket will be valid for the draw dates shown on the front of the ticket. ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "3. DO NOT USE RED INK OR ERASE. Use only blue or black ink or pencil. If you make an error, please fill out a new play slip. Check the play slip carefully before presenting it to the retailer. The player is responsible for the teams and the number of draws selected, not the retailer or the Kansas Lottery. ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
